From: Erik Schnetter <schnetter@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] configure: check for _vsnprintf_l

meson.build checks for `_vsnprintf_l`, but configure.ac does not, so the
Autotools build never defines HAVE__VSNPRINTF_L.  On Windows the
FcStrDupVapFormat chain in src/fcint.h then falls through to the
HAVE_VASPRINTF branch, which calls FcLocaleSetCurrent() -- a function
src/fccompat.c only defines `#ifndef _WIN32`.  The result is a link
failure for libfontconfig:

    fcstr.o: In function `FcStrDupVaFormat':
    src/fcstr.c:121: undefined reference to `FcLocaleSetCurrent'

Check the declaration (with <stdio.h> included, since mingw-w64 provides
`_vsnprintf_l` as an inline function when targeting UCRT) so that Windows
uses the intended locale-argument branch instead.

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -212,6 +212,8 @@
 
 AC_CHECK_DECL([mkostemp],[AC_DEFINE_UNQUOTED([HAVE_MKOSTEMP],[1],[Define to 1 if you have the 'mkostemp' function.])],[],[#include <stdlib.h>])
 
+AC_CHECK_DECL([_vsnprintf_l],[AC_DEFINE_UNQUOTED([HAVE__VSNPRINTF_L],[1],[Define to 1 if you have the '_vsnprintf_l' function.])],[],[#include <stdio.h>])
+
 AC_SEARCH_LIBS([fabs], [m], [], [AC_MSG_ERROR([unable to find the fabs() function])])
 
